# tlo: slub_droga
On Saturday at dawn the bridesmaids unplaited Hanka’s hair – for the last time as a maiden’s – and dressed her in a white blouse and an embroidered bodice, and on her head they set a wreath of rue.{ mak_w_medaliku: Round her neck she hung the locket with the dried poppy.}{ ekwipunek ? krzyzyk: {mak_w_medaliku:Beside it – the iron cross from her father.|Round her neck she hung the iron cross from her father.}}
When she stood in the doorway, Jaromir’s throat went dry. She seemed to him at once a stranger and more his own than ever before.
~ ekwipunek += siekiera
~ siekiera_dziadka = true
Before setting off for church the young couple knelt on the threshold, and their parents blessed them with the sign of the cross and sprinkled them with holy water. Then Jaromir’s father rose from the bench, {noga_ojca == zlamana:leaning on his stick|leaning on his crutches}, and handed his son an axe with a worn, dark haft.
{ figurka_u_staruchy && los_psa == oswojony:
    “Grandfather Maciek’s axe,” he said. “Your grandmother bade me give it to you when you came of age. And so you have. Now you are master here.”
- else:
    { figurka_u_staruchy:
        “Grandfather Maciek’s axe,” he said. “That’s all I had left of him{krzesiwo_dziadka && not krzesiwo_od_babki:, that and the flint and steel,|,} when…” He broke off and cleared his throat. “Now you are master here.”
    - else:
        “Grandfather Maciek’s axe,” he said. “My father left it to me when he was dying. Now you are master here.”
    }
}
{ krzesiwo_dziadka && not krzesiwo_od_babki:
    ~ ekwipunek += krzesiwo
    ~ krzesiwo_na_slubie = true
    To the axe he added a small, blackened flint and steel. “This was his too. He carried it on him to the very end.”
}
They drove to Bukowiec in three carts decked with green sprigs and ribbons. A fiddler and a bass player kept up their tunes the whole way, and the lads cracked their whips till the horses shied again and again. Only on the stretch of road beneath the forest did the music fall silent for a moment, of its own accord, at no one’s bidding, and it struck up again only once the last spruces were left behind. There was a smell of rue from the wreaths, of horse sweat and autumn leaves, and the bells on the harness jingled in time with the bass. # pokaz: wozy
{ kapliczki_drogi == obronil_kapliczke:
    At the surviving shrine Hanka had them stop, and she laid beneath it a sprig of rue from her own wreath.
}
The priest married them in the little wooden church in Bukowiec. {szukanie_franka == rada_babki:Hanka, still hoarse from her night in the reeds, repeated the words of the vow in a whisper|Hanka repeated the words of the vow softly}, but steadily, while Jaromir was so nervous that twice he got her name wrong and everyone in the pews snorted with laughter.
When they got back to Zapadlina, his mother was waiting for them in front of the cottage with bread and salt.{ ekwipunek ? podkowa: Above the door, ends pointing skywards, the smith’s horseshoe already hung.} # dalej
