= oczepiny
# tlo: wesele_noc
The wedding went on late into the night. The band played obertases and krakowiaks till the walls shook; the guests drank, sang and danced on the threshing floor, and on the tables the wedding loaves were heaped high, baked by Hanka with Franek’s honey.{ swaty == po_staremu: Staś led the wedding as master of ceremonies and raised toasts until he was hoarse – louder than he needed to, as if to drown out the fact that he had not slept for a week.| Old Staś was not there. Through Antek he sent back the bottle of vodka with the red ribbon – the same one he had waited with that day by the fence. Unopened.}{ szukanie_franka == antek_sam: Antek turned up only late in the evening, stood in a corner and kept apart from the revelry – but he came.| Antek whirled each of the bridesmaids round in turn, and then drank with Jaromir to the health of the newlyweds and to his brother – in silence, without clinking glasses.}
At midnight came the capping of the bride. The women sat Hanka on the kneading trough, took the wreath from her head and put on a married woman’s cap. Twice she threw it off, as custom demands, until the third time she let them tie it – from that moment she was a wife, no longer a maiden. # pokaz: oczepiny
Jaromir stepped outside for a breath of air. The night was misty, and a chill was drifting from the forest.
Someone was standing at the edge of the woods. # pokaz: starzec
An old man, a head taller than any of the wedding guests, in a sheepskin turned fleece-out and a hat of moss with a broad, drooping brim. He leaned on a knotty staff and nodded gently in time to the obertas that carried from the cottage across the whole field. Beneath the hat only the two bright points of his eyes could be seen.{ poszedl_po_wstazke: Jaromir knew him at once. It was the same old man he had seen in the forest as a boy, when he went after Hanka’s ribbon. He had not aged a single day.}{ ekwipunek ? szczeniak: {imie_psa} pressed against Jaromir’s legs and whimpered softly.}
# pytanie: What will Jaromir do?
*   [Carry him a wedding loaf and a glass from the feast table.]
    ~ weselny_gosc = ugoszczony_kolaczem
    Jaromir went back inside, took a wedding loaf and a full glass from the table, and walked across the field right up to the first spruces. He set them on a stump a few paces from the old man and stepped back. The figure did not so much as stir. # pokaz: kolacz
    When Jaromir looked back from halfway, the stump was bare. The old man nodded to him – slowly, gravely, as one master of a household to another – and vanished into the mist. # pokaz: skinienie # dalej
    -> pierwszy_ranek
*   [Go up and ask what he wants.]
    ~ weselny_gosc = zapytany
    Jaromir set off across the field. The mist grew thicker, and the old man came no nearer at all – as if with every step Jaromir took, he drew back by the same distance. At last Jaromir stopped. # pokaz: mgla
    “What do you want?” he called.
    The voice that answered him soughed like wind in the treetops.
    “You marry well, grandson of Maciek. Watch over her.”
    When the mist cleared, there was no one at the edge of the woods. # pokaz: odszedl # dalej
    -> pierwszy_ranek
