= pierwszy_ranek
# tlo: pierwszy_ranek
~ zapiski += starzec_2
He woke at dawn in the new room he had built onto his father’s cottage over the summer. Hanka slept beside him, her hair spread across the pillow{ ekwipunek ? krzyzyk: and the iron cross at her throat}. Grey, cold light came in through the panes.
He went outside. In the night a hard frost had set in, and the whole yard was white with rime.
Only under the window of the new room was the ground bare and dark. There the white had melted away in a broad oval, as if something large and warm had lain against the wall all night, curled up in a ball. When Jaromir laid his palm on the earth, it was still lukewarm. # pokaz: tropy
Hanka came out after him, a shawl thrown over her shoulders. For a long while she stood over the spot without a word. Then she fetched a handful of ash from the hearth and scattered it over the thawed patch until its shape was blurred away.
“Not a word to anyone,” she said. “Or half the village will come running to gawp, and the other half will say it was you sleeping under the window because I threw you out of the room.” # dalej
